   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(3 + h)^{2} - 9}{h} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 6
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(3 + h) - f(3) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{2} \\), because \\( f(3) = 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": 9
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{2} \\) and the base point is \\( x = 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(3) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 2 x \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(3) = 6 \\).",
         "mathjson": 6
      }
   ],
